# constitution §46 `law.nominal` — SEMANTIC DESCRIPTOR IDENTITY IS INDEPENDENT
# OF PHYSICAL REPRESENTATION. gap[082]'s blocker, gap[097].
#
#     d: feet = 3.0            # d IS feet, and d IS a double
#     d:to(inch)               # reaches the trie, because d carries `feet`
#
# WHAT THIS FIXTURE EXISTS TO CATCH. `d: feet = 3.0` was REJECTED — "variable
# 'd' declared as 'feet', but initializer has type 'f64'" — so a user
# descriptor could not be attached to a value at all. The conversion algebra
# had already landed and was deriving `feet -> micron -> inch`; it was deriving
# edges between descriptors NO RUNTIME VALUE COULD CARRY. The trie could only
# be reached when the call site SPELLED the source (`inch:from(feet)(v)`) or
# when the source was a primitive, which is why 1647 conversion sites in the
# tree reach exactly six destinations. §46 calls this the milestone the algebra
# is waiting on, and it is not a conversion feature: it is representation
# polymorphism.
#
# NO NEW GRAMMAR AND NO NEW TYPE (A2 NNS-FIRST). A named descriptor already
# resolved to a `.@"struct"` identity; what was missing was the REPRESENTATION
# FACT beside it. Nothing was added to the resolved-type union, so no lowering
# path grew an arm it could get wrong — which is exactly what makes the
# zero-overhead claim below provable rather than hoped for.
#
# VERIFIED BY VALUE, and the value is chosen to kill every degenerate answer.
# 3 feet is 36 inches and 914400 micron; the total is 914436. A `feet` that
# silently became a plain f64 and lost its descriptor would find no edge and
# fail to compile. A composition that resolved and returned 0 — this tree's
# known failure mode — prints 914400 or 36. A trie answering from a transposed
# key would not compile. Only a value that really carries `feet`, through a
# hub composition nobody declared AND a declared edge, prints 914436.
# expect: 914436
#
# ZERO PHYSICAL OVERHEAD, and it is checked as a SEPARATE FACT by
# `scripts/nominal_zero_cost.id`, because "it printed the right number" does
# not distinguish a double from a boxed double that happens to add correctly.
# That gate reads the emitted C and requires `double d`, no `lua_Value`, no
# `duo_retain`, and the conversions inlined as direct calls. The first draft of
# this mechanism DID emit `duo_retain((void*)(d))` on a `double`, and only the
# C compiler caught it — a reminder that every switch listing a descriptor as
# boxed is a place a nominal descriptor can quietly acquire a cost.
#
# THE DECLARATION SPELLING IS DEBT, RECORDED NOT HIDDEN. §46's own example is
# `feet: f64`, and that spelling parses today as a BINDING with no initializer
# rather than as a descriptor: `src/parser.zig` mints an `alias_def` from
# `name: type` only when the type is a RECORD. `type feet = f64` is the form
# that reaches the descriptor registry, so it is the form under test here.
# gap[097] owes the one-line parser repair; the mechanism does not depend on
# which spelling declares it.

type micron = f64
type inch = f64
type feet = f64

stretch: f64 = (v: f64)
    v * 25400.0

shrink: f64 = (v: f64)
    v / 25400.0

grow: f64 = (v: f64)
    v * 304800.0

shrivel: f64 = (v: f64)
    v / 304800.0

to(micron)(inch) = stretch@lossless
to(inch)(micron) = shrink@lossless
to(micron)(feet) = grow@lossless
to(feet)(micron) = shrivel@lossless

main: i64 = ()
    # The binding a descriptor could not inhabit. `3.0` carries no descriptor
    # of its own, so CDR (B-13) lets the contract name it — the same rule that
    # makes `n: u8 = 3` a u8. A value that ALREADY carries a descriptor is
    # refused instead; that half is `examples/compile_fail/nominal_bare.id`.
    d: feet = 3.0

    # Subject-first, canonical (§0.5 FACE-CALL). `feet -> inch` was never
    # declared: it is composed through the `micron` hub, and the witness rides
    # inside the emitted artifact.
    n: inch = d:to(inch)

    # The authored edge, so the fixture measures BOTH answers the trie gives.
    q: micron = d:to(micron)

    total = n:to(i64) + q:to(i64)
    print("{total}")
    0
